
Z-machine Randomization Test Suite
by David Griffith 2002 - 2024
This program is in the public domain.
Originally distributed with Frotz.
Release 2 / Serial number 240229

Screen Height: 24
Screen Width:  80

1) Bellcurve graph.
2) Spread graph.
q) Quit.

Please select a test: 

This program drops "balls" from the very top-middle of a vertical two-dimensional field filled with pegs.  The balls bounce off the pegs either left or right until they drop into one of several slots at the bottom where they stack up.  There are one less than half as many levels of pegs as there are slots.  This means that if a ball always bounces left, it will fall the leftmost slot.  Likewise, a ball always bouncing right will fall into the rightmost slot. According to the laws of probability, if the bounces are totally random, a smooth bellcurve should appear when the balls are counted and put into a bar graph.  This program displays such a bar graph.

A ball which settles in the center of the field is represented by '|'.
A ball which settles to the left or right of the center is represented by 'o'.

How many drops (1 through 9) per ball drawn? 

Press any key to begin.  
prev: 0            <space>: pause.
drops: 1           Press 'q' to quit.
granularity: 1



















